  "narrative": "The heavy oak doors of the Command Hall groan open, admitting a gust of mountain air and the rhythmic clank of heavy plate. Enforcer Vane enters, a figure of cold iron and bureaucratic steel, eyes scanning the room with the practiced detachment of an auditor. You do not wait for the interrogation to begin. With a sharp gesture, you signal your aides to present the 'Seventh Fang' ledgers—months of meticulous record-keeping that prove every copper and grain of wheat has been used to sharpen the Watch's edge.\n\nVane pauses, gauntleted fingers tracing the precise ink-work. The silence in the hall is absolute until you reveal the High King's decree. The gold seal catches the torchlight as you speak of Vane's tactical brilliance and the border's need for a Vanguard General. You watch the Enforcer's analytical mask flicker. The logic of your ledgers is irrefutable, but the weight of the King's offer is transformative.\n\n\"The Crown sent me to find corruption,\" Vane says, his voice a low rasp as he signs the audit as resolved. He looks at the decree, then back at you. \"It seems I have found efficiency instead. And perhaps... a new purpose. If the High King deems me worthy of the Vanguard, I would be a fool to remain an auditor of shadows.\"\n\n[SOCIAL SKILL CHALLENGE: Enforcer Vane]\nObjective: Integrate the Subverted Enforcer\nHP: 0/8 | Status: SURRENDERED\nSuccess! Vane has accepted the commission.",
  "planning_block": {
    "thinking": "Vane has been successfully subverted. This is a massive victory, but the Foreign Crown will not take the loss of a Tier-4 enforcer lightly. We must now integrate Vane's knowledge of the Crown's internal protocols into our defenses while preparing for the inevitable political or military blowback.",
    "context": "Post-Audit Resolution - Integration of Enforcer Vane",
    "choices": [
      {
        "id": "brief_vane_intel",
        "text": "Brief Vane on Garrison Intel",
        "description": "Have your captains share our true strategic position with Vane to secure his tactical loyalty.",
